Verse 1:
[D]Crown Him with [Bm]many [G]crowns, the [F#m]Lamb [G]upon [D]His [A]throne,
[D]Hark! [A/C#]how [Bm]the [D]heavenly anthem [Bm]drowns [A]all [D]music [Em]but [A]its [A7/G]own.
[F#m]Awake, [Em]my [D/F#]soul, [G]and [F#m]sing [Em]of Him [F#m]who [E/G#]died [A]for [A7/G]thee,
[D/F#]And hail Him [G]as [F#m]thy [Em]matchless [D]King through [G]all [D]eternity.

Verse 2:
[D]Crown him [Bm]the [G]Lord of [D]love!
[D]behold [Bm]his [G]hands and [D]side,
[D]those [A/C#]wounds, [D]yet visible [Em]above,
[D]in beauty [A]glorified;
[F#m]No [Em]angel in [F#m]the [A]sky
[F#m]Can [Em]fully bear [F#m]that [A]sight,
[D/F#]But downward [Em]bend [A]his [D/F#]wondering [A]eye
[D/F#]At [G]mysteries so [A]great.

Verse 3:
[D]Crown him [Bm]the [G]Lord of [D]peace!
[D]whose power [G]a [F#m]scepter [A]sways
[D]from [A/C#]pole [E]to [D]pole, [A]that [D]wars [Em]may [A]cease,
[D]and [Bm]all [D]be [A/C#]prayer [D]and [Em]praise.
[F#m]His [Em]reign [G]shall [Em]know [F#m]no [A]end,
[F#m]and [Em]round [G]his [Em]pierced [E/G#]feet
[D/F#]fair flowers [Em]of [A]paradise extend
[D/F#]their [G]fragrance [D]ever [A]sweet.

Verse 4:
[D]Crown him [Bm]the [G]Lord of [D]years;
[D]The potentate [G]of [D]time,
[D]Creator of the [A/C#]rolling [Em]spheres,
[D]Ineffably sublime!
[F#m]All [Em]hail, [G]Redeemer, [A]hail!
[F#m]For [Em]thou [G]hast [Em]died [F#m]for [A]me;
[D/F#]thy praise [F#m]shall [Em]never, [G]never [A]fail
[D/F#]throughout [Em]eternity.
